 - [ ] **PREVIEW-003**: When concurrent requests miss the cache for the same preview key, the system SHALL return 202 with the same job ticket and a two-second retry interval while one shared render job is pending.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-004**: When admitting a completed preview would exceed 12 GiB of cached JPEG data, the system SHALL evict entries before admission so the cache remains within that limit.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-005**: When a render job fails, the system SHALL release its deduplication entry so a later request can enqueue a new job.
+
+## Eviction (2Q policy)
+
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-EVICT-001**: When a completed render is admitted and its preview key is not in the ghost list (the keys-only record of recently evicted first-use entries), the system shall insert the new cache entry at the tail of the A1 first-use queue, managed FIFO.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-EVICT-002**: When a completed render is admitted and its preview key is in the ghost list, the system shall admit the entry at the most-recently-used position of the Am main LRU queue and remove the key from the ghost list.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-EVICT-003**: When a cache entry in the A1 queue is accessed again before being evicted, the system shall move that entry to the most-recently-used position of the Am queue, removing it from A1.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-EVICT-004**: When inserting an entry into the A1 queue would push A1's cached JPEG data past its 3 GiB share of the 12 GiB cache budget, the system shall evict the entry at A1's head and add its preview key to the ghost list.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-EVICT-005**: When inserting an entry into the Am queue would push Am's cached JPEG data past its 9 GiB share of the 12 GiB cache budget, the system shall evict Am's least-recently-used entry.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-EVICT-006**: When adding a key to the ghost list would exceed its bound of 2048 keys, the system shall discard the oldest key in the ghost list first.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-EVICT-007**: The ghost list shall hold preview keys only and shall never hold cached JPEG data; total cached JPEG data across A1 and Am shall never exceed 12 GiB.
